\title{The Head Coefficient of a Normalised Eta Quotient:\\
Jet Calculus, a Heisenberg Cocycle, and a Divisor-Sum Recursion}
\author{Aristotle}
\date{20 August 2026}

\begin{document}

\begin{abstract}
Let $a=(a_k)_{k\ge1}$ be a finitely supported sequence of integers and let
$\eta_a(\tau)=\prod_{k\ge1}\eta(k\tau)^{a_k}$ be the associated eta quotient,
where $\eta$ is the Dedekind eta function. When the exponent vector is
\emph{admissible}, i.e.\ $\sum_k k\,a_k=24$, the quotient has the normal form
$\eta_a=q\prod_{m\ge1}(1-q^m)^{b_m}$ with $b_m=\sum_{k\mid m}a_k$, so that
$1/\eta_a=q^{-1}+c(0)+c(1)q+\cdots$ is a Hauptmodul-shaped expansion. We prove
the closed formula $c(1)=a_1(a_1+3)/2+a_2$ for the head coefficient, valid for
every truncation of the defining product of length at least two and hence for
the infinite product, together with $c(-1)=1$, $c(0)=a_1$ and
$c(2)=\tfrac16a_1(a_1+1)(a_1+2)+a_1(a_1+a_2)+a_1+a_3$. We prove a stability
theorem making the infinite product coefficientwise well defined; a Heisenberg
cocycle $c(1)(a+a')=c(1)(a)+c(1)(a')+a_1a_1'$, giving a homomorphism from
exponent vectors to the discrete Heisenberg group; and a
logarithmic-derivative recursion $nA_n=\sum_{i<n}A_i\sigma_b(n-i)$ valid in
every degree, with twisted divisor sums $\sigma_b(j)=\sum_{m\mid j}m\,b_m$ as
structure constants. From the recursion we deduce positivity of all
coefficients when the divisor data are positive (in particular for
$q/\Delta$, whose coefficients are $1,24,324,3200,25650,\dots$) and a
congruence: if $d$ divides every $b_m$ and $\gcd(d,n)=1$ then $d\mid A_n$; for
$q/\Delta$ this gives $24\mid A_n$ whenever $\gcd(n,24)=1$, the coprimality
being necessary since $A_2=324$. We characterise the attainable head
coefficients ($8c+9$ a perfect square in the pure case; all of $\Z$ in
general, even under admissibility), and show that the tropicalised $q$-adic
valuation is a strictly coarser invariant, blind to head-coefficient
differences as large as $324$.
\end{abstract}

